{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Fast train of sorrow Hauling broken hearts like mine
[C]And mighty like a [G]real express It’s pulling down the [D]line
[G]So when you said that we were through I didn’t have to [C]guess
[C]That i was to just [G]ride upon that ole [D]heartbreak [G]express
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]I always knew someday I’d wind [G]up riding down this line
[A]You’re giving me my ticket honey Many many times
[G]Here I am, heading for the land of [C]loneliness
[C]Speeding askew through the [G]darkness on that [D]ole heart break [G]express
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Every time i think of you It fills my heart with pain
I can’t recall just where it was I climbed aboard this train
I looked out and there were all My dreams ah waving by
I knew that i was on this train And hung my head and cried
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Maybe i played around to long With our happiness
Is that how i got thrown upon This ole heartbreak express
I wish i knew how i could throw the switch upon the track
And tell the train just circle round And carry me right back
{end_of_chorus}
